{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>יִשְׁכְּבוּ</b> Three times in the Masorah: טֶרֶם יִשְׁכְּבוּ. עַרְלִים יִשְׁכָּבוּ (Ezekiel 30:22). יַחַד עֲלֵי עָפָר יִשְׁכָּבוּ (Job 10:22). Meaning: \"the uncircumcised shall lie down\" — the gentiles, who are like the men of Sodom, for concerning Sodomites and their like that verse was spoken." "<b>מִקְצֵה</b> Two times in the Masorah: כָּל הָעָם מִקְצֵה. כִּי נִלְכְּדָה הָעִיר מִקְצֵה. In the passage of Nebuchadnezzar, to teach that these are worthy of destruction like those, and further, when they departed from here their city too was captured מִקְצֵה."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:30.759977027Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}